exports[`git.pull.watch, via rhachet given: [case1] a repo with the mechanic role linked when: [t4] get reads a box that holds watches, and unwell daemons then: the tree names the cure for each unwell part 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.pull.watch get
   ├─ daemon v1.0.0+cafe0001 · stale · pid 999999999 · last tick <n>s ago · paused (token locked)
   │  ├─ home: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=1.0.0+cafe0001/bin
   │  └─ watches
   │     ├─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1220 → @:mechanic (surf-demo.beav.feat-wave)
   │     └─ unreadable record: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=1.0.0+cafe0001/watches/surf-demo.1221.json
   └─ daemon v1.0.1+cafe0002 · absent · no pid · never ticked
      ├─ home: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=1.0.1+cafe0002/bin
      └─ watches
         └─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1230 → @:mechanic-two (surf-demo.beav.feat-wave)

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a stale, wedged, or absent daemon serves no watch
      ├─ 1. read why it stopped: cat <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=1.0.0+cafe0001/daemon.log
      └─ 2. start a fresh one: rhx git.pull.watch set --pull <n> --mode apply

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a paused daemon reads naught; the github token is locked
      └─ rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env prep --key EHMPATHY_SEATURTLE_GITHUB_TOKEN

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a watch record that does not parse is held, never served
      ├─ 1. read it: cat <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=1.0.0+cafe0001/watches/surf-demo.1221.json
      └─ 2. rewrite it from its clone: rhx git.pull.watch set --pull <n> --mode apply
"
`;

